//api.github.com/users/jeremyf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyf/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyf/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyf/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyf/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyf/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2019-07-30T14:47:38Z","updated_at":"2022-01-27T12:15:29Z","closed_at":"2022-01-27T12:15:29Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Describe the bug**\r\n\r\nA podcast host recently reported that their podcast on DEV wasn't updating with the newest episodes.\r\n\r\nAfter a deeper look, we realized the episodes in their RSS are sorted from oldest to newest ones, so the latest are at the bottom. Our current logic is to fetch all the episodes when a podcast is created and then check the \"latest\" 5 every hour. We assume the latest podcasts to be the top ones (as it generally is this way for most of the podcasts).\r\n\r\nThus, our logic isn't accounting for times when a user's RSS may be ordered differently.\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior**\r\n\r\nA show's episodes should stay up to date regardless of how articles are ordered in the RSS.\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\n\r\nThis user mentioned possibly using the date tags to sort this out.","closed_by":{"login":"jeremyf","id":2130,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2130?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyf","html_url":"https://github.com/jeremyf","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com